From 48088f2cee4a75d00abfc91d6665bd8ab5b9dc00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W1nkelm4nn <mrmarkap61@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 07:38:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] Emulate geometry shaders with compute stages.

Metal has no geometry stage, and MoltenVK left geometry shaders out of
a pipeline, so whatever they emit was missing, such as particles or the
triangles a shader culls, duplicates or routes to other layers.

Emulate them like tessellation. The vertex shader runs as a compute
kernel and writes its outputs packed into a buffer. The geometry shader
runs as a compute kernel, with one thread per input primitive and
invocation, using the resources of the tessellation control stage. It
writes each vertex it emits, packed the same way, into a fixed range of
slots, along with its index, and ending a primitive writes a restart
index. Rasterization then draws these strips with a vertex shader that
replays the emitted vertices. All three are SPIR-V modules derived from
the vertex and geometry shaders, so they are compiled like any other.
Indirect draws are converted into the arguments of each stage on the
GPU. If an emulated pipeline cannot be compiled, the geometry shader is
left out as before, and MVK_CONFIG_EMULATE_GEOMETRY_SHADERS=0 turns the
emulation off.
---
